---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE_LINKS } from '../lib/config';
---

<BaseLayout title="About — Outside?" description="What Outside? does, who made it, and what it does not check.">
  <article class="prose">
    <h1>About Outside?</h1>
    <p>
      Outside? helps you decide whether to head outside now, and spot a better time in the next 24 hours, for walking,
      running, cycling, hanging out or just being outdoors. Pick a place, optionally pick an activity, and it explains
      how the forecast matches your preferences.
    </p>
    <p>
      Matches are based only on the forecast it shows and the preferences you set. They are not safety advice and do not
      include air quality, UV, pollen or official weather alerts. See <a href="/methodology/">how it works</a> for the
      details and limitations.
    </p>
    <h2>Open source</h2>
    <p>
      The code is open source under the MIT license, so anyone can use, adapt and run their own copy. Weather and location
      data keep their own licenses.{' '}
      {SITE_LINKS.source !== undefined && <> The source code is <a href={SITE_LINKS.source}>available here</a>.</>}
    </p>
    <h2>Who made it</h2>
    <p>
      Outside? is a project by{' '}
      {SITE_LINKS.author !== undefined ? <a href={SITE_LINKS.author}>Naresh Kumar</a> : 'Naresh Kumar'}.
    </p>
    <h2>Data</h2>
    <p>
      Weather data by <a href="https://open-meteo.com/">Open-Meteo</a>, licensed under{' '}
      <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/">CC BY 4.0</a>. Location search uses data from{' '}
      <a href="https://www.geonames.org/">GeoNames</a> via Open-Meteo. The area name for "Use my location" comes from{' '}
      <a href="https://www.bigdatacloud.com/">BigDataCloud</a>. Read the <a href="/privacy/">privacy notes</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
